 "verdict": "PARTLY ATTRIBUTED, AND THE TWO BANDS DIFFER. Overall 23.52% at the release, 13.92% with everything testable switched off. ASK ORDERING falls 20.63% -> 9.74%: their determinized search carries most of it, which is expected -- `V06Agent::resetV6` re-seeds `srng` from the agent seed, so a fresh process per decision draws the same determinizations every turn where their arbiter's stream advances. DECLARATION GATE barely moves, 2.64% -> 4.18%, and it is the band that costs sets. Their tie-breaking contributes nothing (27.96% with it off, against 23.52%), and their own code says why: at rtie=1 the tie RNG is CONSTRUCTED per decision from the public hash and the event count, so it is replayable by construction and only rtie=2 would not be. Ruled out by reading rather than by an arm: their belief consumes no RNG in the released `Fast` mode and `sinkhornDisj` re-initialises from the Knowledge rather than warm-starting; `deadAsk`, `deadInSearch` and `dead7` are all off in the frozen spec, so the dead-ask memory is inert. WHAT THIS MEANS FOR A FIX: the search term would yield to a per-decision seed derived from the event count, but the declaration band would not, and no re-seeding reaches it. A stateless bridge cannot be made honest against this engine by seeding alone (baseline 23.52%, search off 16.61%, ties off 27.96%, both off 15.78%, and their lastMySet feature off too 13.92%).",
 "seconds": 157.0
}
